    EDITS.append(('   **What fit_memory changed for this step.**',
                  '   **fit_memory addendum 4 (incremental notice-prefix encoding, `fit_memory/SPEC_ADDENDUM_4_INCREMENTAL_NOTICE_ENCODING.md`).** The storage_limits loop re-serialized, re-tokenized and re-keyed the whole notice prefix at every origin with a new notice, so it slowed as the prefix grew. fit_memory keeps per-notice texts and token ids, each complete 254-token chunk vector once, and a running text digest. It returns exactly what `encode_cached` returns on the full prefix text: same vectors, encoding dicts with key order, and cache files. Fail-closed checks re-tokenize the real prefix every 500 new corpora and at the last origin. Proof: `fit_memory/A4_PROOF.json`; switch decision: `fit_memory/A4_DECISION.json`.\n\n   **What fit_memory changed for this step.**'))
